WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.190
In many cases, you may find yourself or somebody faking a smile in photos.
很多时候，你可能会发现自己或别人在照片里假笑。

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:13.290
Why can one easily discover a fake smile and why does it seem so difficult to give a real smile in photos?
为什么人们能轻易识破假笑，又为什么在照片里露出真正的笑容似乎这么难？

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:18.650
Scientists have found that a real smile is characterized by two main muscle movements.
科学家发现，真正的笑容以两个主要的肌肉动作为特征。

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:25.330
When we smile, we lift our mouth upwards and cause the skin around our eyes to gather into folds.
我们微笑时，会向上提起嘴角，并使眼睛周围的皮肤聚拢成褶皱。

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.970
These muscle movements are usually absent in the case of a forced smile, especially when the smile is small.
如果是强装出来的笑容，通常就没有这些肌肉动作，尤其是在笑容很浅的时候。

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.290
Our brains are highly skilled at distinguishing the differences in muscle movements.
我们的大脑非常善于分辨肌肉动作上的差异。

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:44.190
That’s why though trying to fake a real smile can be hard, discovering a fake one on someone else is a piece of cake.
正因如此，尽管试图装出真正的笑容可能很难，但要识破别人脸上的假笑却是小菜一碟。

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:50.850
One of the most common reasons why you look unnatural in photos is an increased awareness of your appearance.
你在照片里显得不自然，最常见的原因之一是你更加在意自己的外表了。

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:57.090
The worry about posture, hair, and makeup can add to the stress, killing the chances of a real smile.
对姿势、头发和妆容的担忧可能会加重压力，扼杀露出真正笑容的机会。

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.150
A smile looks best when it comes naturally.
笑容在自然流露时最好看。

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:12.540
Warm and welcoming smiles come along with warm and welcoming body language, but when you’re in front of the camera, trying too hard to perform can make your body language appear stiff and far from welcoming.
温暖亲切的笑容与温暖亲切的肢体语言相伴而来，但在镜头前，表现得太用力，可能会让你的肢体语言显得僵硬，一点也不亲切。

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.230
Besides, facial expressions are not always understood in the same way.
此外，人们对面部表情的理解并不总是一样的。

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.860
A smile can mean different things in different cultures.
笑容在不同的文化中可能有不同的含义。

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:27.570
For example, a wide smile that seems welcoming to some may appear fake and dishonest to others.
例如，一个大大的笑容，在一些人看来很亲切，在另一些人看来却可能显得虚假、不真诚。

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.140
This may also influence how people feel about your smile in photos.
这也可能影响人们对你照片中笑容的感受。

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.350
However, we shouldn’t let this trouble us too much.
不过，我们不应该让这一点过分困扰自己。

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:43.560
So, if you want to smile naturally before the camera, perhaps the simplest trick is to give your brain a real reason to feel happy.
所以，如果你想在镜头前自然地微笑，也许最简单的诀窍就是给大脑一个感到快乐的真正理由。

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.750
Maybe recall a joyful moment or just think back to a funny story you read… that should work!
也许可以回忆一个快乐的时刻，或者就回想一下你读过的某个有趣的故事……这应该会管用！
